The code looks good. A few refinements I want to make:

1. `updateSun(tod)` is called every frame — it does a lot of work (creating new Colors each frame: `new THREE.Color(...)` allocations → GC pressure). Let me optimize: precompute the palette colors and avoid allocations in the loop. `skyPal` creates `new THREE.Color(...)` per call ✗. Let me optimize skyPal to reuse temp colors.

2. The `document.getElementById('prog')` per frame → cache the element.

3. The label update writes styles every frame for 30 labels → acceptable, but let me only update when the camera moves... it's fine.

4. `updateSun` also sets `sun.shadow.camera` — no, it doesn't ✓.

Let me optimize updateSun (avoid per-frame allocations) since it runs 60x/sec.

Let me rewrite skyPal to avoid allocations:

```js
const cTop=new THREE.Color(), cBot=new THREE.Color(), cA=new THREE.Color(), cB=new THREE.Color();
function skyPal(t){
  for(let i=0;i<PAL.length-1;i++){
    if(t>=PAL[i][0]&&t<=PAL[i+1][0]){
      const f=(t-PAL[i][0])/(PAL[i+1][0]-PAL[i][0]||1);
      cTop.setHex(PAL[i][1]).lerp(cA.setHex(PAL[i+1][1]),f);
      cBot.setHex(PAL[i][2]).lerp(cB.setHex(PAL[i+1][2]),f);
      return;
    }
  }
}
```
And in updateSun, avoid `new THREE.Color(...)`:
```js
sun.color.setHex(0xff9c4e).lerp(cA.setHex(0xfff4e2),clamp(el/0.9,0,1));
hemi.color.copy(cTop).lerp(cA.setHex(0xffffff),.35);
hemi.groundColor.setHex(0x3a3226).lerp(cA.setHex(0x6b5a44),dayF);
```
✓ with a single temp color cA.

Also `sun.position.copy(dir).multiplyScalar(340).add(new THREE.Vector3(-45,0,-30))` → allocates a Vector3 per frame → use a constant `const TGT=new THREE.Vector3(-45,0,-30)` ✓.

And `new THREE.Vector3(0,8.5,0)` in the camera code → allocations per frame (3-4 per frame) → acceptable but let me use constants.

Let me apply these micro-optimizations.

5. Another improvement: the initial camera in 'libre' mode when switching from another mode — `controls.target.copy(curPos)` ✓ set on switching ✓.

6. The "restart" button resets u=0 but the camera stays ✓.

7. One more thing: `showStop` has a 260ms setTimeout for the fade — if the user clicks quickly, multiple timeouts could stack. Minor.

8. Also `voiceOn` — the speech synthesis ✓.

Let me apply the optimizations and then do the final test.

Also let me double check the `glowMat.opacity` animation ✓.

One more: the `dash.offset.x` — the texture repeat is 140 along the tube ✓ and the offset animates ✓.

